{title: Whiskey and Gunpowder}
{artist: Red Mesa Drifters}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[A]Daddy kept a bottle w[D]here the bible ought to be
[A]Loaded up his shotgun ev[E]ery time he looked at me
[A]Sheriff's at the door [D]again, the hounds are on the hill
[A]Some men die of f[E]ever, some men d[A]ie of will
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[D]Whiskey and gunpow[A]der
[E]Burning down the famil[A]y name
[D]Whiskey and gunpow[A]der
[E]Every son ends up t[A]he same
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[A]I swore I'd never touc[D]h it, now it's sitting on my shelf
[A]I'm fighting every devil [E]and the meanest one's myself
[A]Mama's in the churchy[D]ard where the cottonwoods grow tall
[A]I'd trade a hundre[E]d bullets just t[A]o hear her call
{end_of_verse}

